            "target_entity_instance": "Poland",
            "target_entity_type": "Country",
            "paragraph": "For instance, in September 2024 in Poland, precipitation exceeded 400 mm over three days, a new record for extreme events (https://hydrobim.pl/en/flood-in-poland-2024/) (Kimutai et al. 2024).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "agricultural droughts",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Poland",
            "target_entity_type": "Country",
            "paragraph": "On the other hand, from 1 May to 30 June 2024, Poland's average Climatic Water Balance (CWB) value was -121 mm, meaning that the total surface evaporation over Poland was 121 mm higher than the precipitation (https://susza.iung.pulawy.pl/en/komentarz/2024,05/). Extremely low CWB values are a symptom of agricultural droughts that frequently evolve into extremely low flows or hydrological droughts, which are increasingly common in Central Europe (Meresa et al. 2016, Piniewski et al. 2022).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "agricultural droughts",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "IS_OF_TYPE",
            "target_entity_instance": "Drought",
            "target_entity_type": "NaturalHazardType",
            "paragraph": "Extremely low CWB values are a symptom of agricultural droughts that frequently evolve into extremely low flows or hydrological droughts, which are increasingly common in Central Europe (Meresa et al. 2016, Piniewski et al. 2022).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "drought",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Central Europe",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Based on several research papers, Central Europe has experienced numerous extreme events in recent decades, and, at the same time, more floods and droughts happen during the year, especially over the warm season (June to September), and these changes could become more frequent in the future (H\u00e4nsel et al. 2019, Hari et al. 2020, Piniewski et al. 2022, Tomczyk et al. 2022, Eini et al. 2023b, Szyga-Pluta et al. 2023, Marcinkowski et al. 2024, Knutzen et al. 2025).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
