            "relation": "IS_OF_TYPE",
            "target_entity_instance": "Drought",
            "target_entity_type": "NaturalHazardType",
            "paragraph": "Recent observations indicate that the Earth's climate is undergoing significant changes. Global temperatures are increasing, precipitation patterns are shifting, and extreme weather events, such as floods and droughts, are becoming more frequent and severe, while glaciers continue to recede (Yin and Sun 2018, Abro et al. 2021, Rojpratak and Supharatid 2022, Vinod and Mahesha 2024, Delavar et al. 2025).",
